From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:44:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WNM: pass the space left in the BSS TM Request buffer to
 mbo_add_ie()

wnm_send_bss_tm_req() passed buf + sizeof(buf) - pos as the space left
for the MBO element. buf is a pointer, so sizeof(buf) is the size of the
pointer, and pos is always past the fixed fields of the frame. The
difference is negative and converts to a size_t near SIZE_MAX, so the
length check in mbo_add_ie() could never fail.

The allocation holds 1000 octets plus the neighbour reports and the MBO
attributes. The header and the fixed fields (31 octets), the BSS
Termination Duration (12) and the Session Information URL (at most 256)
take at most 299 of the 1000, and the MBO element header 6 more, so no
write went past the buffer. Pass the space that is left in the
allocation.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
+++ b/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
@@ -963,6 +963,7 @@ int wnm_send_bss_tm_req(struct hostapd_d
 			const u8 *mbo_attrs, size_t mbo_len)
 {
 	u8 *buf, *pos;
+	size_t buf_len;
 	struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt;
 	size_t url_len;
 	const u8 *own_addr = wnm_ap_get_own_addr(hapd, sta);
@@ -972,7 +973,8 @@ int wnm_send_bss_tm_req(struct hostapd_d
 		   " req_mode=0x%x disassoc_timer=%d valid_int=0x%x dialog_token=%u",
 		   MAC2STR(sta->addr), req_mode, disassoc_timer, valid_int,
 		   dialog_token);
-	buf = os_zalloc(1000 + nei_rep_len + mbo_len);
+	buf_len = 1000 + nei_rep_len + mbo_len;
+	buf = os_zalloc(buf_len);
 	if (buf == NULL)
 		return -1;
 	mgmt = (struct ieee80211_mgmt *) buf;
@@ -1016,7 +1018,7 @@ int wnm_send_bss_tm_req(struct hostapd_d
 	}
 
 	if (mbo_len > 0) {
-		pos += mbo_add_ie(pos, buf + sizeof(buf) - pos, mbo_attrs,
+		pos += mbo_add_ie(pos, buf + buf_len - pos, mbo_attrs,
 				  mbo_len);
 	}
 
